{% comment %}
  One-time purchase escape hatch, shown under the supply options.

  Clicking it is a buy action, not just a selection: the script clears the
  selling plan, sets quantity to 1, and submits the surrounding product form, so
  the plain product goes to the cart on its own.

  Supply is a product option, so the variant is a function of flavour AND supply
  — dropping the plan alone is not enough. Without a supply of its own this link
  would add whichever supply card was last selected, one-time, which reads to a
  shopper as the choice being ignored. Supply Option Value names the size a
  one-time purchase is, and the script resolves it against the flavour the
  shopper is on rather than pinning a variant, so the flavour survives.

  Left blank the link keeps the previously selected supply, which is the old
  behaviour — right for a product whose supply is not a real option.

  Accepts:
  - block {Object} - the onetime block. Reads settings.text and
    settings.supply_value.

  Usage:
  {% render 'CWC_pdp-onetime__block', block: block %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}
  <div class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__onetime" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
    <button
      type="button"
      class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__onetime-button"
      data-cwc-onetime
      {% if block.settings.supply_value != blank %}
        data-cwc-onetime-value="{{ block.settings.supply_value | strip | escape }}"
      {% endif %}
    >
      {{ block.settings.text }}
    </button>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
